From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 07:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add linux-riscv64 from unofficial-builds

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; upstream has not released since 2022]

nodejs.org/dist publishes no linux-riscv64 tarball, but
unofficial-builds.nodejs.org does (from v18.4.0), the same source
make_wheels.py already uses for linux-x64-musl.

Tag it manylinux_2_39_riscv64, not the node binary's own looser
GLIBC_2.28 floor: PyPA publishes no manylinux_riscv64 base image below
2_39 (quay.io/pypa/manylinux_2_39_riscv64, the image this workflow
already builds in; see pypa/manylinux's README), and uv's own riscv64
manylinux floor is 2_31 regardless (see this repo's porting playbook,
gotcha 642), so a 2_28-tagged wheel is simply not a tag any installer resolves
on riscv64 -- `uv pip install` fails every leg with "has no wheels
with a matching platform tag", never reaching the GLIBC check the
tag's number implies.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 make_wheels.py | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/make_wheels.py b/make_wheels.py
--- a/make_wheels.py
+++ b/make_wheels.py
@@ -46,12 +46,13 @@
     'linux-x64':    'manylinux_2_12_x86_64.manylinux2010_x86_64',
     'linux-armv7l': 'manylinux_2_17_armv7l.manylinux2014_armv7l',
     'linux-arm64':  'manylinux_2_17_aarch64.manylinux2014_aarch64',
-    'linux-x64-musl': 'musllinux_1_1_x86_64'
+    'linux-x64-musl': 'musllinux_1_1_x86_64',
+    'linux-riscv64': 'manylinux_2_39_riscv64',
 }

 # https://github.com/nodejs/unofficial-builds/
 # Versions added here should match the keys above
-UNOFFICIAL_NODEJS_BUILDS = {'linux-x64-musl'}
+UNOFFICIAL_NODEJS_BUILDS = {'linux-x64-musl', 'linux-riscv64'}

 _mismatched_versions = UNOFFICIAL_NODEJS_BUILDS - set(PLATFORMS.keys())
 if _mismatched_versions:
